{
  "why": "The cumulative variant of the host side of the gumball tool protocol: a selection record with `gumballCumulative` makes `worldGumballStep` send every `stream` tick and the `commit` as the WHOLE offset from the grab pose (angle, factor) instead of the delta since the previous tick, and the identity while the pose is back on the grab, so each tick is idempotent and a tick the guest drops as stale costs the gesture nothing. A case's `cumulative`, `live`, `transformMode` and `targets` fill its `start` events. A guest that consumes cumulative ticks (fem 3d) replays a case's dispatches with the target ids replaced by one movable node of its own document, then again with each single stream dispatch dropped and again with every stream dispatch dropped, and must publish exactly `guest.edits` edits moving it by `guest.offset` every time. Guests that compose deltas replay `gumball-live-protocol.json` instead.",
